From: djsaunde <1245942+djsaunde@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:14:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] fast: include <array> and <algorithm> in
 interpreter.cpp

interpreter.cpp uses std::array (class template argument deduction) and std::clamp without including
<array> or <algorithm>; it built only while another standard header pulled them in. GCC 13's libstdc++
(Ubuntu 24.04's g++-mingw-w64-i686-posix, the Windows CI job) no longer does: "class template argument
deduction failed" at the std::array tables and "'clamp' is not a member of 'std'".
---
 src/fast/interpreter.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/fast/interpreter.cpp b/src/fast/interpreter.cpp
index f540c20..1a90618 100644
--- a/src/fast/interpreter.cpp
+++ b/src/fast/interpreter.cpp
@@ -18,6 +18,8 @@
 #include <vector>
 #include <list>
 #include <stack>
+#include <array>
+#include <algorithm>
 #include "fast/resource/type/Light.h"
 
 #ifndef _LANGUAGE_C
